// `.oxfmtrc.json` - the formatting half of the oxc pair. oxlint's config is
// references/typescript-oxlintrc.jsonc; two files, two binaries, no shared settings.
// Verified 2026-09-03 against oxfmt 0.65.0 on node 24 (0.66.0 is published; the 4-day
// release-age quarantine holds it back, so `ignorePatterns` is confirmed on 0.65.0 only).
//
//   pnpm add -D oxfmt@0.65.0
//   pnpm exec oxfmt --check .   # gate: exit 1 when a file is unformatted, 0 clean
//   pnpm exec oxfmt .           # `--write` is the default mode, so a bare run rewrites files
//
// WHY THE IGNORE. oxfmt formats more than JS/TS: on 0.65.0 it also reformats `.md`, `.yaml` and
// `.json`. Markdown belongs to rumdl house-wide (`rumdl check`, `rumdl-format`), so leaving it to
// oxfmt puts two formatters on one file - each rewrites the other's output and both `--check`
// gates fail forever. Excluding Markdown here keeps one owner per file type. YAML and JSON stay
// with oxfmt, which has no other owner in this catalogue.
//
// Traps, all verified on 0.65.0:
//   - `ignorePatterns` is the only key in the file `--init` writes, and there is no ignore flag
//     beside `--ignore-path`. That flag REPLACES the default `.gitignore` + `.prettierignore`
//     pair rather than adding to it: with `--ignore-path other.ignore`, a path excluded by
//     `.prettierignore` is formatted again.
//   - Patterns are gitignore-shaped, not glob-anchored: `*.md` and `**/*.md` both exclude nested
//     Markdown. `docs/*.md` excludes one level only.
//   - `--list-different` and `--check` BOTH exit 1 when something is unformatted. `--check` prints
//     statistics, `--list-different` prints one path per file - which is what the canary needs.
//   - A path argument containing `..` is refused outright ("PATH must not contain '..'"), so the
//     gate runs from the repo root over `.`, never from a subdirectory pointing upwards.
//   - `node_modules` is skipped by default; `--with-node-modules` un-skips it.
//   - oxfmt reformats `.oxlintrc.json` and this file too. Comments survive, the layout does not -
//     let it own them (run `oxfmt .` once after dropping either in), or add the paths here.
//   - A pattern matching nothing is silent, so assert the exclusion with the canary below rather
//     than trusting a green run.
{
  "ignorePatterns": [
    "*.md",
    "dist/**",
    "coverage/**",
    "tools/oxlint/anti-slop/**",
    ".agents/**",
    ".claude/**",
    ".codex/**",
    ".cursor/**",
    ".opencode/**",
    ".pi/**"
  ]
}
// CANARY. `oxfmt --check` exits 0 both when Markdown is correctly excluded and when oxfmt never
// looked at the tree at all, so assert on the file list, not the exit code:
//
//   printf '# T\n\n*  a\n' > fmt-canary.md
//   pnpm exec oxfmt --list-different . | grep -q 'fmt-canary.md' && echo "markdown not excluded"
//   rm -f fmt-canary.md
//
// The probe file must be deliberately misformatted (the loose list marker above): a Markdown file
// oxfmt would not change is absent from the list whether or not the ignore works.
